{"type":"data","nodes":[{"type":"data","data":[{"stars":1},1],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"sections":1},[2,8],{"title":3,"pages":4},"",[5],{"title":6,"slug":7},"Introduction","index",{"title":9,"pages":10},"berm",[11,14,17,20,23,26],{"title":12,"slug":13},"Overview","berm/overview",{"title":15,"slug":16},"Writing a Program","berm/writing-a-program",{"title":18,"slug":19},"The Guest API","berm/guest-api",{"title":21,"slug":22},"The Manifest","berm/manifest",{"title":24,"slug":25},"Publishing a Program","berm/publishing",{"title":27,"slug":28},"Running the Service","berm/service"],"uses":{}},{"type":"data","data":[{"slug":1,"title":2,"description":3,"toc":4,"html":39,"prev":40,"next":43},"berm/writing-a-program","Writing a Program","",[5,9,12,15,18,21,24,27,30,33,36],{"depth":6,"id":7,"text":8},2,"public-tools","Public tools",{"depth":6,"id":10,"text":11},"arguments","Arguments",{"depth":6,"id":13,"text":14},"results-and-failure","Results and failure",{"depth":6,"id":16,"text":17},"building","Building",{"depth":6,"id":19,"text":20},"anonymous-calls","Anonymous calls",{"depth":6,"id":22,"text":23},"queries","Queries",{"depth":6,"id":25,"text":26},"crons","Crons",{"depth":6,"id":28,"text":29},"stripe-events","Stripe events",{"depth":6,"id":31,"text":32},"events","Events",{"depth":6,"id":34,"text":35},"calling-another-program","Calling another program",{"depth":6,"id":37,"text":38},"changing-an-interface","Changing an interface","\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>berm-lang\u003C/code> is the guest side. It owns the ABI, so an author never sees a call\nnumber or a pointer pair.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">#![cfg_attr(target_arch \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> \"wasm32\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, no_std, no_main)]\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">extern\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> crate\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> alloc;\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">use\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> alloc\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">::\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">string\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">::\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">String\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">;\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">use\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> berm_lang\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">::\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">Schema\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">;\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">#[berm_lang\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">::\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">program]\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">mod\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> tools\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> {\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    use\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> crate::\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">Echo\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">;\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    use\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> alloc\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">::\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">string\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">::\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">String\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">;\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    use\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> berm_lang\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">::\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">Result\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">;\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">    /// Answers its arguments back.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    #[public]\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    pub\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> fn\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> echo\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">        /// The text to echo back.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">        query\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">:\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> String\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">        /// Page number, zero-indexed.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">        page\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">:\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> Option\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">u32\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">>,\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    ) \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">->\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> Result\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">Echo\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">> {\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">        Ok\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">Echo\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> { query, page })\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">    }\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">}\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">/// What `echo` answers.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">#[derive(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">Schema\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">)]\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">pub\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> struct\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> Echo\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> {\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    pub\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> query\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">:\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> String\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">,\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    pub\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> page\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">:\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> Option\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">u32\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">>,\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">}\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cp>Every \u003Ccode>pub fn\u003C/code> in the module is a tool. Its doc comment is the description the\nmodel reads when deciding whether to call it, so write it for that reader.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>What a program reaches past its arguments — who called, state, a database,\nHTTP, other programs, wakes — is \u003Ca href=\"../guest-api/\">the guest API\u003C/a>.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"public-tools\">\u003Ca href=\"#public-tools\">Public tools\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>A tool is internal unless marked \u003Ccode>#[public]\u003C/code>: only its host calls it, for the\nprogram's own wakes, crons and Stripe events. A \u003Ccode>#[public]\u003C/code> tool is called by\ncallers from outside, as the host authenticates them, and by other programs\nthrough \u003Ccode>berm_lang::call\u003C/code>. \u003Ccode>#[callers(services)]\u003C/code> limits it to other programs,\nand \u003Ccode>#[callers(accounts)]\u003C/code> to callers from outside.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"arguments\">\u003Ca href=\"#arguments\">Arguments\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>A tool's parameters are the properties of its arguments, a JSON object. A\nparameter's doc comment is its description, and an \u003Ccode>Option\u003C/code> parameter may be\nomitted. A tool with no parameters takes any arguments and reads none.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>Each parameter's type implements \u003Ccode>Schema\u003C/code>: strings, numbers, \u003Ccode>bool\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>Vec\u003C/code>,\n\u003Ccode>Option\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>BTreeMap&#x3C;String, T>\u003C/code>, and any type with \u003Ccode>#[derive(Schema)]\u003C/code>, in any\nmodule or crate. The derive takes a struct with named fields — an object titled\nby its name, its fields' doc comments their descriptions — or an enum of unit\nvariants, a string that is one of them in \u003Ccode>snake_case\u003C/code>. A \u003Ccode>Schema\u003C/code> type owns\nits data, and the derive gives it serde's \u003Ccode>Serialize\u003C/code> and \u003Ccode>Deserialize\u003C/code>.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"results-and-failure\">\u003Ca href=\"#results-and-failure\">Results and failure\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>A tool returns \u003Ccode>berm_lang::Result&#x3C;T>\u003C/code>. \u003Ccode>T\u003C/code> is a \u003Ccode>Schema\u003C/code> type, written as the\nJSON result and declared in the manifest as \u003Ccode>returns\u003C/code>; \u003Ccode>()\u003C/code> writes nothing. An\nabsent \u003Ccode>Option\u003C/code> field is left out rather than written as \u003Ccode>null\u003C/code>.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>Err(berm_lang::Error)\u003C/code> reports failure through the ABI, its \u003Ccode>message\u003C/code> the\ncaller's to read. It is not a trap: the host sees a tool that ran and failed. A\nsyscall's \u003Ccode>CallError\u003C/code> and a \u003Ccode>String\u003C/code> convert into it, so \u003Ccode>?\u003C/code> reports either. An\nenum marked \u003Ccode>#[error_code]\u003C/code>, each variant with \u003Ccode>#[msg(\"…\")]\u003C/code>, converts into it\nwith that message. \u003Ccode>berm_lang::deny(message)\u003C/code> fails the call as denied.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"building\">\u003Ca href=\"#building\">Building\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>A program is a crate with one bin target and \u003Ccode>berm-lang\u003C/code> as a dependency:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">rustup\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> target\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> add\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> wasm32-unknown-unknown\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">cargo\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> new\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> --lib\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> my-program\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">cd\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> my-program\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">cargo\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> add\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> berm-lang\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">[[\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">bin\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">]]\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">name = \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"my-program\"\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">path = \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"src/bin/main.rs\"\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cpre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// src/bin/main.rs\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">#![cfg_attr(target_arch \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> \"wasm32\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, no_std, no_main)]\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">extern\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> crate\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> my_program \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">as\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> _;\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">#[cfg(not(target_arch \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> \"wasm32\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">))]\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">fn\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> main\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">() {}\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>cargo build --release --target wasm32-unknown-unknown\u003C/code> writes the image to\n\u003Ccode>target/wasm32-unknown-unknown/release/my-program.wasm\u003C/code>.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>The tools live in \u003Ccode>src/lib.rs\u003C/code> under a three-line\n\u003Ccode>src/bin/main.rs\u003C/code> that does nothing but \u003Ccode>extern crate\u003C/code> them, because cargo emits\nan image for a bin target and an archive for a lib — the library alone never\ngets linked, and the binary alone cannot be reached from \u003Ccode>tests/\u003C/code>.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>Off a guest target the crate is an ordinary library, so tools can be unit tested\nnatively instead of cross-compiling to run anything at all. \u003Ccode>berm_lang::test\u003C/code>\nstands in for the host: it holds the argument blob and collects what a program\nlogged. A call reaching a syscall that has no stand-in panics naming it,\nrather than reading a plausible zero.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>berm_host::test::TestHost\u003C/code>, behind \u003Ccode>berm-host\u003C/code>'s \u003Ccode>test\u003C/code> feature, runs the built\nimage instead: the real engine and host, with fetches answered from what the\ntest arranged, a clock the test sets, and wakes the test fires. A call's result\nand meter, the logs and state it committed, and the wakes it armed are read back\nfrom it.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>berm-fixture\u003C/code> in this repository is the worked example — the smallest real\nprogram, and what berm's own tests run against.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"anonymous-calls\">\u003Ca href=\"#anonymous-calls\">Anonymous calls\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>A call from outside with no caller — no account, or an app's call with no\nuser — reaches only a tool marked \u003Ccode>#[anonymous]\u003C/code>, and the host refuses it any\nother. An \u003Ccode>#[anonymous]\u003C/code> tool is \u003Ccode>#[public]\u003C/code>, and not \u003Ccode>#[callers(services)]\u003C/code>.\n\u003Ccode>berm_lang::caller()\u003C/code> answers \u003Ccode>None\u003C/code> in it for such a call.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"queries\">\u003Ca href=\"#queries\">Queries\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>#[query]\u003C/code> marks a tool read-only. While it runs, and in every call it makes,\n\u003Ccode>berm.set\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>berm.emit\u003C/code> and \u003Ccode>berm.call.after\u003C/code> are refused, so it leaves nothing\nfor the host to commit. A host may serve it over \u003Ccode>GET\u003C/code>.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"crons\">\u003Ca href=\"#crons\">Crons\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>#[cron]\u003C/code> marks a tool its host calls each time its cron expression fires,\nwhatever the last call ended as, and not while its owner is held. A cron tool\ntakes no parameters and is not \u003Ccode>#[public]\u003C/code>. Its expression is five fields,\nminute to day of week, read in UTC: \u003Ccode>*/5 * * * *\u003C/code>. The deploy sets it, or its\nowner does while it runs; until one is set it is not called.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"stripe-events\">\u003Ca href=\"#stripe-events\">Stripe events\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>#[stripe]\u003C/code> marks the tool its host calls with each Stripe event its daemon\ntakes for the program, and not while its owner is held. The event object is the\nargument object, so the tool's parameters are the event's fields it reads. A\nprogram has at most one, and it is not \u003Ccode>#[public]\u003C/code>.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"events\">\u003Ca href=\"#events\">Events\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>An \u003Ccode>#[event]\u003C/code> struct anywhere in the program's crate is a typed log, and a\n\u003Ccode>Schema\u003C/code> type. \u003Ccode>berm_lang::emit!(Noted { word })\u003C/code> emits it under the topic\n\u003Ccode>Noted\u003C/code>, its data the struct as JSON. The manifest lists each event under\n\u003Ccode>events\u003C/code> with its doc comment and the schema of its fields.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>Logs are what a program's developer reads to debug it: the host keeps each one beside the call it was emitted in, whatever that call ended as, for 30 days. A log holds at most 4 KiB, its data and topics together, and is refused past that. A program's data goes in its database, read by other programs through its query tools.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"calling-another-program\">\u003Ca href=\"#calling-another-program\">Calling another program\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>The IDL of the program deployed as \u003Ccode>hn\u003C/code>, which its host serves, is saved as\n\u003Ccode>idls/hn.json\u003C/code>. \u003Ccode>berm_lang::declare_program!(hn)\u003C/code> reads it from the crate's directory or the\nnearest ancestor with an \u003Ccode>idls/\u003C/code>, and generates:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cul>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>hn::types\u003C/code>: every titled object and string enum in its tools' arguments and\nresults.\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>hn::calls\u003C/code>: one function per tool, taking its arguments in the IDL's key\norder, an optional one as an \u003Ccode>Option\u003C/code>, and returning its result (\u003Ccode>()\u003C/code> for a\ntool with none).\u003C/li>\n\u003Cli>\u003Ccode>hn::NAME\u003C/code>, which every call names.\u003C/li>\n\u003C/ul>\n\u003Cp>A tool the IDL marks \u003Ccode>deprecated\u003C/code> is generated with \u003Ccode>#[deprecated]\u003C/code>.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"changing-an-interface\">\u003Ca href=\"#changing-an-interface\">Changing an interface\u003C/a>\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>A tool's callers were built against its IDL. A change that breaks them — see\n\u003Ca href=\"../manifest/#compatibility\">the manifest\u003C/a> — keeps the old tool beside the new\none, marked \u003Ccode>#[deprecated]\u003C/code>, until no caller uses it.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>The IDL is a file in the crate; it changes only when it is saved again.\u003C/p>",{"title":41,"slug":42},"Overview","berm/overview",{"title":44,"slug":45},"The Guest API","berm/guest-api"],"uses":{"params":["slug"]}}]}
